\c 2
\s1 Nevukadnetsar's dream
\rem /s1 Daniel's wisdom; Nebuchadnezzar's Dream
\p
\v 1 \add Back in\add* the second year¦356721 of¦356721 King¦356724 Nevukadnetsar's¦356724 \add !(Nebuchadnezzar¦356724)\add* reign¦356723, \add *the¦356726 king¦356726\add* had had some dreams¦356727 that troubled¦356728 him—leaving him unable to sleep¦356730.
\v 2 \add *He\add* summoned¦356736 the¦356737 magicians¦356737, fortune-tellers, sorcerers¦356739, and¦356740 \add ≈astrologers\add* to \add ≈explain\add* the dreams¦356743 to \add *him\add*, so¦356744 they¦356744 came¦356744 in and¦356745 stood¦356745 in¦356746 front¦356746 of¦356746 the¦356747 king¦356747.
\v 3 “I've¦356753 had¦356753 a dream¦356753,” the¦356751 king¦356751 told¦356749 them¦356750, “and my¦356755 spirit¦356755 is¦356754 \add ≈anxious to¦356756 understand¦356756\add* \add *it\add*.”
