\v 10 \add My now\add* the¦359448 queen¦359448\f + \fr 5:10 \ft Possibly ‘the previous queen’, i.e., the queen mother (as the next verse displays her knowledge of past events).\f* had heard about¦359450 what the¦359451 king¦359451 and¦359452 his¦359452 noblemen¦359452 had been saying, so she¦359455 came¦359455 into¦359455 the¦359458 banquet¦359454 house¦359453 and¦359459 said¦359459, “Long live¦359462 the¦359460 king¦359460. Don't¦359463 let¦359465 \add ≈this get under your skin\add*. Don't¦359468 let¦359470 \add ≈it drain you\add*.
