\v 10 \add ≈However although\add* Daniyel¦360139 knew¦360141 that \add ≈that law had been¦360144 passed\add*, he¦360146 \add still\add* went¦360146 into his¦360147 house¦360147 (with the windows¦360148 in¦360151 his¦360151 \add ≈upper¦360151 room¦360151\add* open¦360149 toward Yerushalem¦360153 \add !(Jerusalem¦360153)\add*), and¦360154 he¦360157 continued to kneel¦360159 three¦360155 times¦360154 a day¦360156 to pray¦360163 and¦360164 \add ≈give thanks\add* to God¦360166, \add just\add* as¦360167 he'd¦360172 \add ≈always done¦360173\add*.
\p
\v 11 Then¦360181 those¦360183 \add ≈officials\add* went¦360184 as¦360184 a¦360184 group¦360184 and¦360185 found¦360185 Daniyel¦360186 \add ≈praying to his god¦360190 and presenting him with his¦360190 requests\add*.
\v 12 Then¦360193 they¦360194 approached¦360194 the¦360198 king¦360198 and \add ≈reminded him about the law\add*, “Didn't¦360203 you \add ≈introduce a law\add* that¦360206 within thirty¦360222 days¦360221, any man¦360209 who¦360210 makes a petition to any¦360215 god¦360217 or man¦360218, except¦360223 to you¦360224, \add ≈your¦360225 majesty¦360225\add*, must¦360226 be¦360226 thrown¦360226 into¦360227 the¦360228 lions'¦360228 den¦360227?”
\p “\add ≈Yes, that's correct\add*,” answered the¦360230 king¦360230. “It can't be revoked \add now\add* according¦360234 to¦360234 the¦360234 law¦360234 of¦360234 the¦360236 Madim¦360236 and¦360237 Persians.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦360244 they \add ≈informed\add* the¦360248 king¦360248, “Daniyel¦360250 who¦360251 was¦360252 exiled¦360255 from Yehudah¦360257 \add !(Judah¦360257)\add*, \add ≈pays no attention\add* to¦360261 you¦360261, \add ≈your¦360263 majesty¦360263\add*, or to¦360265 the¦360267 \add ≈law that¦360268 you¦360269 introduced\add*, because he¦360273 petitions¦360274 \add his god\add* three¦360271 times¦360270 a day¦360272.”
\p
\v 14 When¦360277 the¦360278 king¦360278 heard¦360281 \add ≈that\add*, was¦360283 very¦360282 upset and¦360285 \add ≈for that entire day, he¦360287 actively tried to¦360289 think of¦360291 a way to¦360295 get Daniyel¦360286 out of it\add*.
\v 15 \add ≈However, the¦360299 group¦360301 of men¦360299 returned¦360301\add* to¦360302 the¦360304 king¦360304 and¦360305 said¦360305, “You know¦360307, \add ≈your¦360308 majesty¦360308\add*, that¦360309 it's a law¦360311 of¦360312 the¦360312 Madim¦360312 and¦360313 Persians, that¦360314 no rule or law that¦360320 the¦360322 king¦360322 establishes¦360323 can be changed¦360325.”
