\v 16 \add ≈So\add* the¦360329 king¦360329 \add ≈gave an order¦360330\add*, and¦360331 Daniyel¦360332 was brought¦360331 in and the¦360338 king¦360338 responded¦360337 and¦360339 told \add *him¦360340\add*, “May your¦360341 god¦360341, who¦360342 you¦360343 serve \add ≈continually¦360348\add*, save¦360350 you.” Then¦360328 Daniyel¦360340 was¦360345 thrown¦360333 \add down\add* into the¦360336 lions'¦360336 den¦360334.
\v 17 A¦360354 stone¦360354 was¦360353 brought¦360353 and¦360356 laid¦360356 over¦360357 the¦360359 opening¦360359 of¦360359 the¦360360 den¦360360, and¦360361 the¦360362 king¦360362 sealed¦360361 it¦360361 with¦360363 his¦360363 own signet ring and¦360364 with¦360364 the¦360364 signet¦360364 rings¦360364 of¦360364 his¦360365 nobles¦360365 so that¦360366 \add ≈no one¦360355 could sneak Daniyel¦360371 out\add*.
