\v 21 “\add ≈Long live¦360440\add* the king,” Daniyel¦360433 \add ≈called back\add*.
\v 22 “My¦360443 god¦360443 sent¦360444 his¦360445 angel¦360445 and¦360446 shut¦360446 the¦360448 lions'¦360448 \add #mouths¦360447\add*, and¦360449 they¦360450 haven't hurt¦360450 me¦360450, because¦360453 \add ≈he saw¦360457 that¦360454 I\add* \add ^wasn't guilty of anything\add*. Also¦360459, \add ≈your¦360462 majesty¦360462\add*, I¦360465 haven't \add ≈wronged you in any way\add*.”
\p
\v 23 Then¦360468 the¦360469 king¦360469 was¦360471 very¦360470 happy, and¦360473 ordered¦360474 that¦360491 Daniyel¦360473 be pulled up¦360475 out of the¦360478 den¦360478. So¦360479 Daniyel¦360480 was¦360479 lifted¦360479 out of the¦360483 den¦360483, and¦360484 \add ≈he didn't¦360487 even have a scratch\add* on¦360490 him¦360490, because he¦360492 had¦360492 trusted¦360492 in¦360493 his¦360493 god¦360493.
\v 24 \add Then\add* the¦360497 king¦360497 \add ≈ordered¦360496 the arrest of\add* the¦360499 men¦360499 who¦360501 had¦360503 maliciously accused Daniyel¦360506, and \add ≈had them and their wives¦360512 and children¦360511 thrown¦360509\add* into¦360507 the lions' den—they¦360510 didn't¦360513 \add even\add* reach¦360515 the¦360516 bottom¦360516 of¦360516 the¦360517 den¦360517 before the¦360523 lions¦360523 overpowered them and¦360524 \add ≈tore them to pieces¦360504\add*.
\p
\v 25 Then¦360530 King¦360532 Dareyavesh¦360531 \add !(Darius¦360531)\add* wrote¦360533 to¦360534 all¦360534 the¦360536 peoples¦360536, nations¦360537, and¦360538 \add ≈ethnic groups right across his kingdom\add*: “May you all¦360543 \add ≈be enjoying peace¦360546 and prosperity\add*.
\v 26 I decree¦360554 that¦360555 \add ≈everyone¦360557 throughout\add* my¦360560 kingdom¦360560 is¦360561 to \add ≈obey and¦360564 respect¦360564\add* Daniyel's¦360571 god, because he is the \add ≈eternal\add*, living¦360577 God. His kingdom \add ≈will¦360584 never\add* be¦360584 destroyed¦360584, and¦360585 his¦360585 \add ≈rule will continue forever\add*.
\v 27 He¦360591 delivers¦360591 and¦360592 rescues¦360592, and¦360593 he¦360593 does¦360593 \add ≈all kinds of miracles\add* in¦360596 the¦360596 heavens¦360596 and¦360597 on¦360597 earth¦360597. He's¦360599 rescued¦360599 Daniyel¦360600 from¦360601 the¦360603 \add ≈strength and power\add* of¦360603 the¦360604 lions¦360604.”
\p
\v 28 \add ≈So¦360607\add* Daniyel¦360607 prospered¦360609 during¦360610 the¦360610 reign¦360610 of¦360610 Dareyavesh¦360611 and¦360612 during¦360612 the¦360612 reign¦360612 of¦360612 Koresh¦360613 \add !(Cyrus¦360613)\add* the¦360614 Persian.
\c 7
\ms1 Daniyel's visions
\mr (7:1–12:13)
\s1 Daniyel's vision of four creatures
\rem /s1 Daniel's Vision of Four Beasts; Daniel's Vision of the Four Beasts; Visions of the Four Beasts; Daniel's visions; Daniel's Dream of Four Beasts
\p
\v 1 \add Previously,\add* in¦360618 Babylonian King¦360621 Belshatsar's¦360620 \add !(Belshazzar¦360620)\add* first year¦360618, Daniyel¦360623 had seen¦360625 a¦360624 dream¦360624 and¦360626 visions¦360626 in his¦360627 mind¦360627 while lying on¦360628 his¦360630 bed¦360630. Then¦360631 he¦360633 wrote¦360633 the¦360634 dream down and \add ≈gave a summary of¦360634 it\add*.
\v 2 \add *He¦360639\add* \add ≈explained\add*:
\p In¦360643 my¦360643 vision¦360643 at night¦360646 I was looking¦360641, and¦360647 \add ≈suddenly\add*, the¦360648 four¦360648 winds¦360649 were¦360651 stirring¦360651 up¦360651 the¦360652 massive ocean¦360652,
\v 3 and¦360655 four¦360655 huge¦360657 creatures¦360656, each one different¦360662 from the other, were¦360658 coming¦360658 up¦360658 out of \add *it\add*.\x + \xo 7:3: \xt Rev 13:1; 17:8.\x*
\li1
\v 4 The¦360668 first¦360668 \add one\add* was¦360669 like¦360669 a¦360669 lion¦360669\x + \xo 7:4-6: \xt Rev 13:2.\x* but¦360670 had the wings¦360670 of¦360671 an¦360673 eagle¦360673. \add ≈But as I¦360676 watched¦360675, its¦360681 wings were¦360680 torn¦360680\add* off¦360680, and¦360682 it¦360682 was¦360682 lifted¦360682 \add ≈up\add* and¦360686 made¦360690 to¦360690 stand¦360690 on¦360686 two¦360688 feet¦360688 like¦360689 a¦360689 man¦360689, and then¦360691 it¦360693 was¦360693 given¦360693 a \add ≈human\add* \add ≈mind¦360691\add*.
\li1
\v 5 The second¦360699 creature¦360697 resembled a¦360701 bear¦360701 \add ≈with one¦360704 arm raised¦360705\add*. \add ≈It¦360705 was¦360705 chomping on\add* three¦360706 ribs¦360707 and¦360712 it was¦360713 told¦360713 to¦360714 go and \add ≈gorge itself\add* on \add more\add* meat¦360717.
\li1
\v 6 \add ≈Next I¦360723 saw¦360722 another¦360725 creature¦360739 that¦360721 resembled\add* a¦360726 leopard¦360726, \add ≈but¦360727\add* with four wings \add ≈(like¦360726 birds'¦360732 wings) attached to\add* its¦360735 back¦360735, and¦360737 with four¦360737 heads¦360738. \add ≈It¦360741 was¦360741 given¦360741 the authority to¦360742 rule¦360740 people\add*.
\li1
\v 7 The¦360749 final creature¦360751 that¦360745 I¦360747 saw¦360746 in¦360748 the¦360748 \add #vision¦360748\add* was¦360754 dreadful¦360754 and¦360755 terrifying¦360755. It was extremely¦360757 strong¦360756 with large¦360763 iron¦360761 teeth¦360758 and it was¦360764 devouring¦360764 \add >things\add* then trampling¦360769 and crushing¦360765 the¦360766 remainder¦360766. \add ≈Another difference¦360771 from¦360772 the¦360776 other creatures¦360776 was¦360778 that it¦360778 had ten¦360780 horns¦360779 on its head\add*.\x + \xo 7:7: \xt Rev 12:3; 13:1; 17:3.\x*
\p
\v 8 While I¦360784 was¦360784 considering¦360783 the¦360785 horns¦360785, \add ≈suddenly\add* another¦360788 horn, a little¦360789 one, came¦360790 up¦360790 among¦360791 \add ≈the others\add* and¦360793 three¦360793 of¦360794 the¦360796 first horns¦360796 \add ≈that were¦360798 in its way got pulled completely out\add*. \add ≈Incredibly\add*, this¦360810 \add new\add* had eyes¦360805 like¦360806 a person¦360807 and¦360811 a¦360811 mouth¦360811 \add ≈that had a lot of incredible¦360813 things to say¦360812\add*.\x + \xo 7:8,11: \xt Rev 13:5.\x*
\rem /s1 The revelation of God concerning the one not die
\rem /s1 Judgment before the Ancient One; The Vision of the One Who Has Been Living Forever
\q1
\v 9 I¦360816 kept looking¦360815 \add in the vision\add* while thrones¦360819 were¦360820 set¦360820 up\x + \xo 7:9: \xt Rev 20:4.\x* and¦360821 the ancient¦360821 \add ≈one\add* took his seat. His¦360824 clothing¦360824 was¦360827 as white¦360827 as snow¦360826, and¦360828 his hair¦360828 \add looked\add* like¦360830 pure¦360831 wool¦360830.\x + \xo 7:9: \xt Rev 1:14.\x* His¦360832 throne¦360832 was¦360833 \add ≈flaming¦360833 with\add* fire¦360836, \add and\add* its¦360837 wheels¦360837 were¦360838 burning¦360838 fire¦360839.
\v 10 A¦360841 river¦360841 of¦360842 fire¦360844 was¦360845 coming¦360846 out¦360846 and flowing¦360845 \add ≈along in¦360849 front¦360849 of¦360849\add* him¦360849. Thousands¦360850 and thousands¦360851 served¦360853 him¦360853, and¦360854 myriads¦360854 upon myriads¦360855 were¦360858 standing¦360858 \add ≈in¦360857 front¦360857 of¦360857\add* him¦360857.\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Rev 5:11.\x* The¦360859 court¦360859 sat¦360860 \add in session\add* and¦360861 the documents were¦360862 opened¦360862.\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Rev 20:12.\x*
\p
\v 11 Then¦360866 I continued looking because of¦360869 the \add ≈amazing things\add* that¦360872 the¦360873 horn¦360873 was¦360874 saying¦360874. I¦360876 kept looking until¦360877 that¦360878 \add final\add* creature¦360880 was¦360879 killed¦360879 and¦360881 its¦360882 body¦360882 destroyed¦360881 \add ≈in\add* the¦360884 fire¦360885.
\v 12 As for the other creatures¦360888, their¦360890 \add ≈authority to rule¦360890\add* was taken¦360889 away, but¦360891 an extension¦360891 of life¦360892 was¦360893 given¦360893 to¦360894 them¦360894 for a¦360897 season¦360897 and¦360898 a¦360898 time¦360898.
\p
\v 13 I¦360901 was¦360901 looking¦360900 in¦360902 the¦360902 visions¦360902 of¦360902 the¦360903 night¦360903, and¦360904 \add ≈suddenly\add*, \add ≈someone like¦360909 a¦360909 human¦360910 male\add* was coming¦360911 with the¦360907 clouds¦360907,\x + \xo 7:13: \xt Mat 24:30; 26:64; Mrk 13:26; 14:62; Luk 21:27; Rev 1:7,13; 14:14.\x* and he came to¦360913 the¦360915 ancient¦360915 \add ≈one\add* and¦360918 was presented¦360919 to him¦360919.
\v 14 He was¦360922 given¦360922 \add ≈authority to rule\add* and¦360924 \add ≈splendour¦360924\add* and¦360925 a¦360925 kingdom¦360925, so¦360926 that all¦360926 the¦360927 peoples¦360927, nations¦360928, and¦360929 \add ≈ethnic groups\add* will serve him. His¦360932 \add ≈authority will¦360938 never end\add*, and¦360939 his kingdom \add ≈will¦360943 never\add* be¦360943 destroyed¦360943.\x + \xo 7:14: \xt Rev 11:15.\x*
\s1 The meaning of the visions
\rem /s1 Daniel's Visions Interpreted; The Interpretation of the Dream; The Visions Are Explained; The Vision Is Explained
\p
\v 15 As for me, Daniyel¦360949, my¦360947 spirit¦360947 was¦360946 distressed¦360946 inside¦360950 me, and¦360952 the visions¦360952 in my¦360953 \add ≈mind¦360953\add* kept alarming¦360954 me¦360954.
\v 16 I¦360956 approached¦360956 one¦360959 of¦360960 those \add >who were\add* standing¦360962 there and¦360963 asked¦360964 him¦360966 \add ≈what was going on\add*, so¦360972 he¦360972 told¦360972 me¦360974, and¦360975 then he revealed the¦360975 interpretation¦360975 of¦360975 those things to¦360977 me¦360977:
\mi
\v 17 Those¦360979 four large¦360981 creatures¦360980, they¦360983 represent four \add ≈kingdoms\add* that¦360982 will¦360987 \add ≈come to be¦360984 in the¦360990 world¦360990\add*,
\v 18 \add ≈but¦360992\add* the¦360994 \add ≈dedicated¦360994 followers\add* of¦360994 the¦360995 highest¦360995 one will¦360992 receive¦360992 the¦360993 kingdom¦360993, and¦360996 they¦360996 will¦360996 \add ≈take¦360996 possession¦360996 of¦360996\add* the¦360997 kingdom¦360997 forever¦361002.
\p
\v 19 \add ≈But I¦361006 still wanted¦361006 to¦361007 know more\add* about¦361008 the¦361011 fourth¦361011 creature¦361010 that¦361012 was¦361014 different¦361015 from¦361016 all¦361018 the others, absolutely dreadful¦361020, with its¦361022 iron¦361026 \add #teeth¦361022\add* and¦361027 bronze¦361030 claws¦361027, and which¦361012 devoured¦361031, then¦361005 crushed and¦361033 trampled¦361036 down with¦361034 its¦361034 feet¦361034 what was¦361036 left.
\v 20 \add ≡I also wanted to know\add* about¦361038 the¦361040 ten¦361041 horns on¦361043 its¦361043 head¦361043, and¦361044 the other horn¦361044 that¦361045 came¦361046 up¦361046 later, with three¦361053 \add other\add* horns¦361053 falling¦361047. That horn¦361054 had eyes¦361056 and¦361058 a¦361058 mouth¦361058 that said¦361059 amazing things, and¦361061 it looked \add ≈stronger\add* than¦361063 the others.
\v 21 I¦361068 kept watching, and¦361069 that¦361070 horn¦361069 was¦361071 waging war¦361072 with¦361073 those followers and¦361076 \add ≈gaining over\add* them¦361077\x + \xo 7:21: \xt Rev 13:7.\x*
\v 22 until¦361079 the¦361083 ancient¦361083 \add one\add* arrived¦361082 and¦361085 \add ≈judged¦361085 in favour of¦361087 his followers\add*. Then¦361089 the¦361089 time¦361089 arrived¦361090 when¦361091 \add *they\add* took¦361092 possession¦361092 of¦361092 the¦361093 kingdom¦361091.\x + \xo 7:22: \xt Rev 20:4.\x*
\p
\v 23 Then he¦361096 said¦361096:
\mi The¦361097 fourth creature¦361097 will be a¦361099 fourth kingdom¦361099 in the¦361103 world¦361103 which¦361104 will¦361105 be¦361105 different¦361105 from¦361106 all¦361108 the¦361110 \add other\add* kingdoms¦361110. It¦361111 will¦361111 devour¦361111 the¦361114 whole world¦361114, and¦361115 trample¦361115 it¦361115 down¦361115 and¦361116 crush¦361116 it¦361116.
\v 24 As for the¦361118 ten horns¦361118, ten kings¦361123 will¦361124 \add ≈become prominent\add* in that kingdom¦361121,\x + \xo 7:24: \xt Rev 17:12.\x* and¦361125 then another¦361125 \add ≡king\add* will¦361126 appear. He will¦361129 be¦361129 different¦361129 from¦361130 the¦361132 previous¦361132 \add ≡kings¦361123\add*, and¦361133 he¦361135 will¦361135 \add ≈overcome\add* three¦361133 \add *of them\add*.
\v 25 He¦361141 will¦361141 speak¦361141 \add ≈out\add* against the highest¦361143 one and will¦361144 wear¦361144 out¦361144 the highest¦361139 one's \add ≈followers\add*. He¦361145 will¦361145 intend¦361145 to¦361146 change¦361146 the times¦361147 and¦361148 the law¦361148, and¦361149 \add indeed\add* \add ≈he'll be¦361149 allowed to\add* for a¦361153 two times¦361154 and¦361155 a half¦361155.\x + \xo 7:25: \xt Rev 12:14; 13:5-6.\x*
\v 26 But¦361158 the¦361158 court¦361158 will¦361159 sit¦361159, and¦361160 then his¦361160 \add ≈authority to rule¦361160\add* will¦361161 be taken¦361161 away—to¦361162 \add ≈perish and¦361163 be forever destroyed¦361163\add*.
\v 27 Then¦361168 the¦361168 kingdom¦361168 and¦361169 the¦361169 \add ≈authority to rule¦361169\add* and¦361170 the¦361170 greatness¦361170 of¦361171 the kingdoms¦361172 under¦361173 all¦361174 the¦361176 heavens¦361176 will be¦361177 given¦361177 to¦361178 the¦361178 people¦361178 \add ≈who are the¦361179 followers\add* of¦361179 the¦361180 highest¦361180 one.\x + \xo 7:27: \xt Rev 20:4.\x* His¦361181 kingdom will \add ≈continue forever¦361183\add*,\x + \xo 7:27: \xt Rev 22:5.\x* and¦361184 all¦361184 \add ≈earthly rulers\add* will¦361187 serve and¦361188 obey¦361188 him.
\p
\v 28 \add ≈That's everything that I¦361197 saw\add* \add in my visions\add*. As for me, Daniyel¦361198, my¦361201 thoughts¦361201 \add ≈made me¦361202 very¦361199 upset\add* and¦361203 my¦361203 face turned¦361204 pale, \add ≈but¦361206\add* I¦361208 kept¦361208 the matter \add ≈to myself\add*.
\c 8
\s1 Daniyel's sheep and goat vision
\rem /s1 Daniel's Vision of a Ram and Goat; Daniel's Vision of a Ram and a Goat; Vision of a Ram and a Goat
\p
\v 1 In¦361211 the third year¦361211 of¦361214 King¦361215 Belshatsar's¦361214 \add !(Belshazzar¦361214)\add* reign¦361213, I¦361219, Daniyel¦361220, had \add ≈another\add* vision¦361216—\add different from\add* the¦361222 previous one.
\v 2 In¦361227 the vision¦361227, I saw that¦361233 I was¦361231 at the¦361232 fortress¦361232 in¦361231 Shushan¦361231 \add !(Susa¦361231)\add* (\add often called Shushan,\add* in¦361234 Eylam province¦361235), beside the¦361242 Ulay¦361243 Canal¦361242.
\v 3 Then¦361245 I¦361245 \add ≈looked¦361247 up¦361245\add*, and \add ≈to my¦361246 surprise, there was\add* a¦361250 ram¦361250 standing¦361252 beside the¦361254 canal¦361254. It¦361255 had two¦361256 horns¦361256 and¦361257 both¦361257 horns¦361257 were¦361258 long, but¦361259 one¦361259 was¦361260 longer than¦361261 the¦361263 other, and¦361264 the¦361264 longer one \add ≈had grown¦361265\add* last¦361266.
\v 4 I¦361268 saw¦361268 the¦361271 ram¦361271 charging westward¦361273, and¦361274 northward¦361274, and¦361275 southward¦361275—no animal¦361278 could stand¦361281 \add ≈against it¦361282\add*—there¦361283 was¦361283 no one¦361284 to rescue¦361284 \add ≈anything from¦361285 it¦361286\add*. \add *The ram\add* did¦361286 \add ≈whatever it wanted, and¦361288 it¦361288 became very powerful\add*.
\p
\v 5 As I was¦361292 observing¦361293, suddenly a billy goat¦361297 was¦361298 coming¦361298 from¦361299 the¦361301 west¦361301, \add ≈crossing the¦361304 entire¦361305 world¦361307\add* without touching¦361309 the¦361310 ground¦361310. The¦361311 goat¦361311 had a¦361312 prominent horn¦361312 between¦361314 its¦361315 eyes¦361315.
\v 6 ⇔In a powerful¦361331 rage¦361330, it charged at the two-horned ram¦361320 that¦361323 I¦361324 had¦361324 seen¦361324 standing¦361325 in¦361326 front¦361326 of¦361326 the¦361327 canal¦361327.
\v 7 I¦361333 saw¦361333 \add @the¦361333 furious¦361333 goat¦361333\add* \add ≈reach\add* the¦361337 ram¦361337 and strike¦361340 it, shattering \add @the ram's\add* two¦361347 horns¦361348. The ram¦361353 \add ≈wasn't strong enough to¦361354 stay standing¦361354 so¦361356\add* it¦361356 was knocked to the ground¦361357 and¦361358 trampled¦361358 on—there was¦361361 no one who could rescue¦361362 the ram¦361363 from¦361364 \add @the¦361364 goat's¦361364\add* \add ≈power\add*.
\p
